#! name: named sources
# named-sources.beatscript: a track put together from sources named with `use` (CC0). Original.
# Four sources from the repo, each named on a line of its own and then used as the program's own: the passacaglia template's
# ground (Holst's five-beat Mars ostinato under its chords, in G minor), the techno genre template's drop, Beethoven's Ode to Joy
# (moved from D into A minor's relative C major, as a role would move it), and Blake's "Tyger! Tyger! burning bright" from the
# phrasebook, sung on the tune. `expand` writes every line out; `check` says what each name is.
tempo 110
key am

use template(passacaglia).ground as ground
use genre@1 techno.drop as drop
use theme ode_to_joy as tune
use phrase @tyger_burning_bright as tyger

# verse: the tune on a piano over a four-on-the-floor kick, the tyger line sung on it
section verse 8 bars {
  deck A: kick x ~ ~ ~ x ~ ~ ~ x ~ ~ ~ x ~ ~ ~ | hihat ~ x ~ x
  deck B: melody tune inst=piano
  deck B: sing tyger on melody voice=robot-choir
}

arrange {
  ground verse
  ~ tune_* rot 2
  drop verse
  @ tune_* oct 1
  verse ground
}
